                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Gary, thanks for the fix. I have some thoughts inline.\n\nRegarding:\n\n> Raising PLDM_FIRMWARE_MAX_STRING to 255 is a separate change that affects struct sizes across the firmware update ABI \u2014 I think that warrants its own patch with maintainer input.\n\nIt warrants its own patch, however the ABI concern is not yet great because the only functions using the struct are marked `LIBPLDM_ABI_TESTING`. While that's the case we can make changes as we see fit.\n\nHowever, 64 was chosen as a \"reasonable\" value for static storage in the context of the library's use in freestanding embedded environments, and so changes do warrant some discussion."
                },
